 `filename`: Name of the file to save the slot's prompt cache. The file will be saved in the directory specified by the `--slot-save-path` server parameter.
 
+When the slot has recurrent or sliding-window rewind checkpoints, the server also writes `filename.checkpoints`.
+Keep this sidecar together with the target snapshot and any `.draft` and `.spec` sidecars when moving or deleting a saved slot.
+The reported byte count includes the sidecars.
+Rewind state can be large, up to the checkpoints already retained by `--ctx-checkpoints`; exact-prefix continuation does not require it.
+Older snapshots without this optional sidecar remain loadable, but recurrent models may need full prompt reprocessing if the resumed prompt diverges before the saved endpoint.
+The sidecar binds checkpoints to the serialized prompt and checks positions, lengths, and a checksum before exposing them to decoding.
